1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,430
You chug a whole

2
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:02,733
pot of coffee...

3
00:00:02,733 --> 00:00:03,400
so what happens

4
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,860
if you never sleep?

5
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:05,860
Day by day...

6
00:00:05,860 --> 00:00:07,551
all the way to day eleven:

7
00:00:07,551 --> 00:00:08,745
the record nobody

8
00:00:08,745 --> 00:00:10,700
is allowed to try anymore.

9
00:00:10,743 --> 00:00:11,684
His cat sleeps

10
00:00:11,684 --> 00:00:12,733
most of the day.

11
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:13,978
So he'll be the champion

12
00:00:13,978 --> 00:00:15,533
of NOT sleeping.

13
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,120
Eleven days?

14
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,782
How hard can it be?

15
00:00:18,997 --> 00:00:20,060
Very.

16
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,330
Hour sixteen.

17
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:22,710
Every hour you're awake,

18
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:23,710
a chemical piles up

19
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:24,827
in your brain...

20
00:00:24,827 --> 00:00:26,100
and the bigger the pile,

21
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,733
the sleepier you feel.

22
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:29,808
Coffee doesn't clear the pile.

23
00:00:29,808 --> 00:00:30,955
It plugs the sensors

24
00:00:30,955 --> 00:00:31,930
that feel it...

25
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:32,525
like tape

26
00:00:32,525 --> 00:00:34,240
over a warning light.

27
00:00:34,291 --> 00:00:35,862
He's not less tired.

28
00:00:35,862 --> 00:00:37,362
He just can't see it.

29
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,164
Hour seventeen.

30
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,265
In one study,

31
00:00:40,265 --> 00:00:42,020
seventeen hours awake

32
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:43,973
hit people like a few drinks...

33
00:00:43,973 --> 00:00:45,447
right at the drink-drive limit

34
00:00:45,447 --> 00:00:47,233
in a lot of countries.

35
00:00:47,284 --> 00:00:48,831
He hasn't had a drop.

36
00:00:48,831 --> 00:00:49,644
He just buttered

37
00:00:49,644 --> 00:00:50,920
his phone.

38
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:52,177
Hour twenty-four.

39
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:53,759
The sun comes up...

40
00:00:53,759 --> 00:00:55,433
and he feels great?

41
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:56,642
That's a trap.

42
00:00:56,642 --> 00:00:57,433
His body clock

43
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:59,283
is ringing the morning bell...

44
00:00:59,283 --> 00:00:59,835
but the pile

45
00:00:59,835 --> 00:01:01,300
hasn't gone anywhere.

46
00:01:01,339 --> 00:01:02,229
And his feelings

47
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:04,060
are turned way up.

48
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,698
After one sleepless night,

49
00:01:05,698 --> 00:01:06,969
the brain's alarm center

50
00:01:06,969 --> 00:01:09,020
fired about sixty percent harder

51
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:10,990
at upsetting pictures.

52
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:11,824
He's sobbing

53
00:01:11,824 --> 00:01:13,551
at a cereal ad.

54
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,933
It's a really nice cereal.

55
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:17,091
Hour thirty.

56
00:01:17,091 --> 00:01:18,840
And now it gets spooky.

57
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,044
Little patches of his brain

58
00:01:20,044 --> 00:01:21,410
start falling asleep...

59
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:23,000
while he's still awake.

60
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:26,489
A microsleep.

61
00:01:26,489 --> 00:01:28,290
A few seconds,

62
00:01:28,290 --> 00:01:28,909
gone.

63
00:01:28,909 --> 00:01:31,080
And the scary part?

64
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,267
You usually don't notice.

65
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,330
On a couch,

66
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:35,267
that's funny.

67
00:01:35,299 --> 00:01:37,280
At the wheel...

68
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:39,467
it's how people crash.

69
00:01:39,689 --> 00:01:40,489
And that...

70
00:01:40,489 --> 00:01:42,189
was the easy part.

71
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:43,300
Day two.

72
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,550
He's freezing.

73
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:45,653
He's starving...

74
00:01:45,653 --> 00:01:47,067
mostly for donuts.

75
00:01:47,092 --> 00:01:48,950
And his brain keeps whispering:

76
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:51,133
just one little nap?

77
00:01:51,190 --> 00:01:51,992
Day three.

78
00:01:51,992 --> 00:01:53,554
The edges of things

79
00:01:53,554 --> 00:01:55,101
start to wobble.

80
00:01:55,344 --> 00:01:57,390
The floor breathes.

81
00:01:57,462 --> 00:01:58,089
And the coat

82
00:01:58,089 --> 00:01:59,000
on the door...

83
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:03,067
turns its head.

84
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:03,698
Seeing things

85
00:02:03,698 --> 00:02:04,437
that aren't there

86
00:02:04,437 --> 00:02:05,642
is a classic effect

87
00:02:05,642 --> 00:02:07,367
of days without sleep.

88
00:02:07,406 --> 00:02:09,260
He's fairly sure...

89
00:02:09,631 --> 00:02:10,391
the cat just told him

90
00:02:10,391 --> 00:02:11,770
to go to bed.

91
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:12,376
Could anyone

92
00:02:12,376 --> 00:02:14,070
really reach day eleven?

93
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:15,167
Someone did.

94
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:16,080
San Diego,

95
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:17,530
nineteen sixty-four:

96
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:18,490
Randy Gardner,

97
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:19,436
seventeen,

98
00:02:19,436 --> 00:02:21,067
for a school science fair.

99
00:02:21,104 --> 00:02:22,149
A sleep scientist

100
00:02:22,149 --> 00:02:22,940
from Stanford

101
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:23,821
came to watch.

102
00:02:23,821 --> 00:02:25,183
Within days,

103
00:02:25,183 --> 00:02:26,646
Randy was moody,

104
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:27,966
forgetful...

105
00:02:27,966 --> 00:02:29,448
and seeing things.

106
00:02:29,674 --> 00:02:30,775
To keep him awake,

107
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,970
they played pinball all night.

108
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:34,081
And Randy...

109
00:02:34,081 --> 00:02:36,633
kept beating the scientist.

110
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:37,762
Day eleven.

111
00:02:37,762 --> 00:02:38,326
They asked him

112
00:02:38,326 --> 00:02:39,855
to count down from a hundred,

113
00:02:39,855 --> 00:02:41,270
in sevens.

114
00:02:41,475 --> 00:02:42,680
A hundred...

115
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:44,590
ninety-three...

116
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,025
eighty-six...

117
00:02:47,025 --> 00:02:48,460
seventy-nine...

118
00:02:48,795 --> 00:02:50,875
seventy-two...

119
00:02:50,875 --> 00:02:52,167
sixty-five...

120
00:02:54,115 --> 00:02:55,295
He stopped.

121
00:02:55,628 --> 00:02:56,075
He'd forgotten

122
00:02:56,075 --> 00:02:57,567
what he was doing.

123
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:58,663
Eleven days

124
00:02:58,663 --> 00:03:00,461
and twenty-four minutes.

125
00:03:00,510 --> 00:03:01,163
Then he slept

126
00:03:01,163 --> 00:03:02,755
for about fourteen hours...

127
00:03:02,755 --> 00:03:04,400
and woke up fine.

128
00:03:04,425 --> 00:03:05,277
So our hero goes

129
00:03:05,277 --> 00:03:06,762
to sign the record book...

130
00:03:06,762 --> 00:03:07,579
and finds out

131
00:03:07,579 --> 00:03:09,730
it stopped letting anyone try.

132
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:10,900
Here's why.

133
00:03:10,925 --> 00:03:12,309
In the nineteen-eighties,

134
00:03:12,309 --> 00:03:14,599
scientists kept rats awake

135
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:15,667
for good.

136
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,610
Within weeks,

137
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:17,490
they were dead...

138
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:18,513
and nobody could say

139
00:03:18,513 --> 00:03:20,133
exactly why.

140
00:03:20,173 --> 00:03:21,322
In twenty-twenty,

141
00:03:21,322 --> 00:03:22,074
a Harvard lab

142
00:03:22,074 --> 00:03:23,624
tried it with fruit flies...

143
00:03:23,624 --> 00:03:25,440
and found the damage piling up

144
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:28,333
somewhere nobody expected.

145
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:29,983
Not the brain.

146
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:31,367
The gut.

147
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:31,954
Mop it up

148
00:03:31,954 --> 00:03:33,419
with antioxidants...

149
00:03:33,419 --> 00:03:35,860
and flies that barely slept

150
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:37,860
lived normal lives.

151
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:39,820
So what is sleep for?

152
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:40,730
One idea:

153
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:41,853
while you sleep,

154
00:03:41,853 --> 00:03:43,364
fluid rinses your brain

155
00:03:43,364 --> 00:03:44,800
like a dishwasher.

156
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:46,140
That's in mice...

157
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,713
and a newer mouse study

158
00:03:47,713 --> 00:03:49,710
found the opposite.

159
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:52,827
Scientists are still arguing.

160
00:03:52,897 --> 00:03:54,870
But here's the weirdest part.

161
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:57,600
Jellyfish seem to sleep too...

162
00:03:57,662 --> 00:03:58,270
and they don't

163
00:03:58,270 --> 00:04:00,267
even have a brain.

164
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:01,265
So sleep may be

165
00:04:01,265 --> 00:04:02,870
older than brains...

166
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:04,139
and life has never found

167
00:04:04,139 --> 00:04:05,833
a way to skip it.

168
00:04:07,996 --> 00:04:09,756
So he does the bravest thing

169
00:04:09,756 --> 00:04:11,649
a record chaser can do.

170
00:04:11,649 --> 00:04:14,016
He goes to bed.

171
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:15,151
Turns out the champion

172
00:04:15,151 --> 00:04:16,620
of this house...

173
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:18,400
was asleep the whole time.

174
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:23,010
Next week:

175
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:23,790
what happens when you

176
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:25,470
hold your breath.

177
00:04:25,470 --> 00:04:26,628
Subscribe...

178
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:27,870
then breathe.

